{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774301276,"nonce":"5LD+LNlkfoHh0XExff5O6GRrhhA=","message":"**Implementation spec**\n\n## Design decisions\n- Extend PropertiesPanel to detect analysis node selection and render a dedicated section\n- Analysis detection: check if selected node type matches known analysis classes (AbstractAnalysis subclasses)\n- Fig ops rendered as an ordered list with type label, params, and drag-to-reorder handles\n- Final ops rendered similarly below fig ops\n- Port configuration shows dependency wiring (which inputs feed from which analysis outputs)\n- Reuses existing UI patterns: section headers with uppercase tracking, input styling, border-t dividers\n\n## Components\n- `FigOpsSection.tsx`: Renders fig_ops as ordered list items with:\n  - Type label (map_figs_at_level, combine_figs_by_level, then_transform_figs, etc.)\n  - Configuration fields: level, dependency_name, metadata\n  - Drag handle via GripVertical icon (visual only for now; DnD library integration deferred)\n- `FinalOpsSection.tsx`: Rendered within FigOpsSection for final_ops_by_type\n- PropertiesPanel modified: adds analysis-specific sections when node spec includes analysis metadata\n\n## Data flow\n- Analysis node spec carries: fig_ops (array), final_ops_by_type (map), dependency ports\n- PropertiesPanel reads these from nodeSpec and renders FigOpsSection\n- Updates go through graphStore.updateNodeParams","files":null}]}